From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] serial: 8250_dw: respect the DT clock-frequency

uart_read_port_properties() already parses "clock-frequency" into
port->uartclk. Do not overwrite it with clk_get_rate() when the DT
provides an explicit rate. This is needed on the Allwinner A733, where
the UART baud clock is the fixed 24 MHz bus clock and the CCU clock
rate reported by the kernel may not reflect the hardware.

Signed-off-by: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c
@@ -719,7 +719,7 @@ static int dw8250_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(data->clk))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(data->clk),
 				     "failed to get baudclk\n");
 
-	if (data->clk)
+	if (data->clk && !p->uartclk)
 		p->uartclk = clk_get_rate(data->clk);
 
 	/* If no clock rate is defined, fail. */
